meta {
  name: 07 - Create Thread
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/threads
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {}
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:2024
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.thread_id) {
    bru.setVar("threadId", res.body.thread_id);
  }
}

docs {
  Requests 01-06 above all used POST /runs/wait, which is *stateless* -
  LangGraph creates and discards an ephemeral thread internally for you.
  
  Real usage (e.g. a chat that needs to remember earlier turns, or a run
  you want to inspect/resume later) goes through a persistent thread
  instead: create one here, then run the graph *on* that thread id in
  request 08.
  
  The post-response script above saves `thread_id` from this response into
  a Bruno variable (threadId), so request 08 can reuse it automatically -
  just run 07 then 08 in order, no copy-pasting needed.
}
